# Sakrylle API Integration

**Default baseUrl must be `https://api.sakrylle.com/v1`.** Paths append directly (normalized by `normalizeBaseUrl`).

| Mode | Path | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| Images | `POST images/generations` | Text-to-image |
| Images | `POST images/edits` | Reference / mask edit (multipart) |
| Responses | `POST responses` | Agent + streaming images |
| Platform | `GET me` | User info / balance / groups (v2) |
| Platform | `GET account/balance` | Legacy v1 fallback |
| Platform | `GET models` | Model list (group-scoped) |

## Auth paths

1. **OAuth PKCE** (recommended) — token for platform API + OAuth Bearer fallback for images/responses
2. **Manual API Key** — stored in IndexedDB profile

**OAuth Bearer fallback** (`oauthFallback.ts`): only when logged in + Sakrylle official baseUrl + no explicit apiKey. Scopes: `images:create` or `image_generation` for Images; `responses:create` for Responses.

**Multi-group** (`groupSelection.ts`): Images and Responses can use different groups. Persisted in `sakrylle-image-playground.selected-groups`.

## Build-time env vars

| Variable | Fallback |
|---|---|
| `VITE_DEFAULT_API_URL` | `https://api.sakrylle.com/v1` |
| `VITE_SAKRYLLE_PLATFORM_API` | → `VITE_DEFAULT_API_URL` |
| `VITE_SAKRYLLE_OAUTH_BASE` | `https://sub.sakrylle.com` |
| `VITE_SAKRYLLE_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID` | `sakrylle-image-playground` |
| `VITE_SAKRYLLE_OIDC_ENABLED` | `false` |

Docker runtime injection via `deploy/inject-api-url.sh`. Production: browser connects directly to `api.sakrylle.com` (no container nginx proxy).

Platform calls use `sakrylleAccount.ts::authedFetch` (401 retry + token injection).
